codemap 9
tour tour-links
kind flow
author ai
group map
note How a step names another tour that documents what its lines call, so shared code and work handed to another process are mapped once and read in place. The link is a field of the step, set by step-link and checked by Map::set_link: the target must exist and cannot be the step's own tour. Renaming a tour rewrites every link to it, a tour that something links to cannot be removed, and check fails on a link to a missing tour. tour --inline and the GUI document show the linked tour inline under the step.

